WEBVTT

STYLE
::cue(c.color9CD5FF) { color: #9CD5FF; }
::cue(c.colora8c7fa) { color: #a8c7fa; }

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:07.000 line:5% align:center
<b><c.color9CD5FF>One Pace Premium</c></b>
Keep the project alive: <c.colora8c7fa>ko-fi.com/not6ip</c>

2
00:00:19.590 --> 00:00:24.960
I grabbed hold, digging in my claws
te ni totte tsume o tateta

3
00:00:24.960 --> 00:00:28.390
but the future
sono mirai wa

4
00:00:28.390 --> 00:00:34.570
blurred together, colors running
nijimu iro ni kasunde mieta

5
00:00:34.570 --> 00:00:41.210
A red that can swallow even summer's hues
natsu no iro mo nuritsubusu you na aka ni

6
00:00:41.310 --> 00:00:47.930
bokura no koe kakikesareteiku you de
now attempts to blot out our voices

7
00:00:47.930 --> 00:00:54.670
Move those halting feet of yours
tachidomaru sono ashi o fumidasou ze

8
00:00:54.670 --> 00:01:01.310
Don't let stand the lies for show
misekake no uso yarisugosu yori

9
00:01:01.310 --> 00:01:07.560
I'll give up countless mornings for my vows
nandome no asa chikai to hikikaeru yo

10
00:01:07.560 --> 00:01:16.110
For the dream that we shared
bokura ga miteita yume

11
00:01:31.360 --> 00:01:36.080
<b>What Death Means</b>

12
00:01:38.890 --> 00:01:40.730
It’s so quiet...

13
00:01:40.730 --> 00:01:42.600
Are they done partying?

14
00:01:43.440 --> 00:01:45.900
Sounds like they stopped
after just one round of drinks.

15
00:01:47.730 --> 00:01:50.860
I didn’t expect Luffy would feel so down...

16
00:01:51.320 --> 00:01:55.910
I need you to take me away
from Egghead-quasar!

17
00:01:55.910 --> 00:01:59.370
It’s true that we failed to
meet our objective, but still...

18
00:02:00.830 --> 00:02:03.160
It’s frustratin’, for sure.

19
00:02:03.160 --> 00:02:07.500
But we had the Five Elders,
a Marine Admiral, CP0, the Seraphim,

20
00:02:07.500 --> 00:02:09.380
and warships surrounding all that!

21
00:02:09.380 --> 00:02:12.550
I’m still tryin’ to wrap my head
around it!

22
00:02:12.550 --> 00:02:16.050
It’s a miracle we even got away
from that total hell, you know?

23
00:02:16.050 --> 00:02:18.510
I absolutely agree with you.

24
00:02:18.510 --> 00:02:22.680
Talk about pathetic...
He’s an Emperor now,

25
00:02:22.680 --> 00:02:25.100
yet he’s mopin’ about one geezer dying.

26
00:02:25.100 --> 00:02:26.980
Oh, c’mon...

27
00:02:35.320 --> 00:02:37.370
All Seraphim to the ship
after recharging!

28
00:02:37.370 --> 00:02:40.280
As for the Sea Beast Weapons
and Pacifista Mk. IIIs...

29
00:02:44.750 --> 00:02:46.460
Rob Lucci! Kaku!

30
00:02:47.130 --> 00:02:48.920
Huh? Where is Stussy?

31
00:02:51.800 --> 00:02:53.380
I killed her.

32
00:02:53.380 --> 00:02:54.470
What?!

33
00:02:59.850 --> 00:03:02.810
What we set out to claim
is now in our hands.

34
00:03:02.810 --> 00:03:06.520
York, Punk Records, the Power Plant...

35
00:03:07.150 --> 00:03:09.860
This puts obtaining the Mother Flame
within our reach.

36
00:03:09.860 --> 00:03:12.860
This will suffice, for now.

37
00:03:13.780 --> 00:03:14.820
However...

38
00:03:15.280 --> 00:03:16.780
We deeply apologize, Sir!

39
00:03:16.780 --> 00:03:20.740
We nine Vice Admirals
led the Buster Call...

40
00:03:20.740 --> 00:03:24.700
But we blundered, allowing the Straw Hats
and Jewelry Bonney to escape!

41
00:03:25.160 --> 00:03:27.670
We’ll proceed to Elbaph from here, Sir!

42
00:03:29.250 --> 00:03:31.130
Do not bother with Elbaph.

43
00:03:32.960 --> 00:03:37.800
If any blunder was committed here,
it was allowing Vegapunk’s broadcast to play.

44
00:03:38.430 --> 00:03:40.510
I never would have imagined...

45
00:03:41.640 --> 00:03:44.520
It is ironic that not only
could we not stop the broadcast,

46
00:03:44.970 --> 00:03:48.020
but that it was the iron giant...

47
00:03:48.020 --> 00:03:51.980
which helped the pirates escape.

48
00:03:51.960 --> 00:03:56.130
Roughly 200 years ago

49
00:03:53.020 --> 00:03:54.610
But St. Saturn!

50
00:03:54.610 --> 00:03:56.740
We were ordered to dispose of it!

51
00:03:56.130 --> 00:03:56.300
Roughly 200 years ago

52
00:03:56.740 --> 00:03:59.780
In the unlikely event they find out,
I will cover for you.

53
00:03:59.780 --> 00:04:00.870
You will study it.

54
00:04:00.870 --> 00:04:01.910
Uh?

55
00:04:01.910 --> 00:04:04.240
That thing is the future.

56
00:04:04.240 --> 00:04:06.750
Researching it will
benefit the military in time.

57
00:04:06.750 --> 00:04:08.330
Thank you, Sir!

58
00:04:08.330 --> 00:04:11.040
We’re deeply interested in it, as well!

59
00:04:11.040 --> 00:04:16.300
Since then, it had not moved even once,
and two hundred years have passed.

60
00:04:16.300 --> 00:04:17.840
But...

61
00:04:17.840 --> 00:04:22.930
it clearly moved
to protect Straw Hat Luffy!

62
00:04:22.930 --> 00:04:24.260
St. Saturn.

63
00:04:25.310 --> 00:04:28.390
I want to ask you something
as a sailor serving the Government.

64
00:04:29.100 --> 00:04:31.020
You called it a “blunder”...

65
00:04:31.020 --> 00:04:32.980
Does that mean...

66
00:04:32.980 --> 00:04:36.900
what Vegapunk said is true?

67
00:04:41.110 --> 00:04:42.990
Vice Admiral Doberman!

68
00:04:42.990 --> 00:04:45.660
I want our medics on their feet, now!

69
00:04:50.290 --> 00:04:51.750
What’s all...?

70
00:04:52.120 --> 00:04:54.250
Island clouds?

71
00:04:55.170 --> 00:04:55.960
Aw, crud!

72
00:04:58.380 --> 00:05:01.840
Why’re there so many?!

73
00:05:04.390 --> 00:05:08.350
Is the Cloud Plant malfunctioning?!
What’s goin’ on?

74
00:05:12.230 --> 00:05:13.230
Oh, I get it!

75
00:05:15.610 --> 00:05:20.440
That you, Edison?!
You didn’t die in the Fabriophase?!

76
00:05:20.440 --> 00:05:21.780
Oops, busted.

77
00:05:36.500 --> 00:05:38.590
Dammit...

78
00:05:39.050 --> 00:05:40.550
He tricked me!

79
00:05:41.720 --> 00:05:43.510
Punk Records...

80
00:05:45.220 --> 00:05:47.050
has been taken away!

81
00:05:48.620 --> 00:05:52.880
Holy
 Land
Mary
Geoise

82
00:05:51.350 --> 00:05:52.890
What does this mean-eh?!

83
00:05:52.890 --> 00:05:55.100
Is what Vegapunk said true?!

84
00:05:55.100 --> 00:05:58.230
Where is Akainu?!
How will he answer for Kuma’s mess?!

85
00:05:58.230 --> 00:06:01.740
Even if the world sinks,
it won’t affect the Holy Land, but...

86
00:06:01.740 --> 00:06:04.700
We-We don’t have a lot of food-eh!

87
00:06:04.700 --> 00:06:08.030
Hey, Chef. I asked for beef-eh.

88
00:06:08.030 --> 00:06:09.790
What’s this fish doing here?!

89
00:06:09.770 --> 00:06:12.980
Growwwl

90
00:06:09.790 --> 00:06:12.980
Forgive me, my lord.
We’ve run out...

91
00:06:13.460 --> 00:06:15.880
I’ve never been so...

92
00:06:16.380 --> 00:06:18.290
humiliated-eh!

93
00:06:19.300 --> 00:06:22.260
We’re facing... a severe food shortage!

94
00:06:22.260 --> 00:06:26.930
I reluctantly skipped one meal
and even a snack yesterday!

95
00:06:26.930 --> 00:06:29.720
What?! That’s a diet fit for prisoners!

96
00:06:29.720 --> 00:06:32.220
Famine?! We’ll starve to death!

97
00:06:32.220 --> 00:06:34.230
We must kill the person who is in charge!

98
00:06:34.230 --> 00:06:37.860
We must punish and admonish the peasants!

99
00:06:37.860 --> 00:06:40.400
This is due to their negligence
and mismanagement-eh!

100
00:06:41.210 --> 00:06:47.170
Hall
 of
 Autho-
rity

101
00:06:45.650 --> 00:06:47.200
Hey! What do you think you’re doing here...

102
00:06:47.570 --> 00:06:48.740
Garling?

103
00:06:51.540 --> 00:06:53.910
I have just received orders...

104
00:06:54.410 --> 00:06:56.290
What orders? Whose?

105
00:06:56.290 --> 00:06:58.670
Care to explain your tone, Garling?

106
00:06:58.670 --> 00:06:59.880
Know your place.

107
00:07:02.920 --> 00:07:07.470
Going forward, Vegapunk York
is to be under my direct command...

108
00:07:09.090 --> 00:07:12.350
and I shall assume the role of
Godhead of Science and Defense.

109
00:07:15.770 --> 00:07:17.060
Impossible!

110
00:07:19.190 --> 00:07:20.980
The world’s entering a time of turmoil...

111
00:07:20.980 --> 00:07:24.360
An unprecedented period of turbulence.

112
00:07:24.360 --> 00:07:28.200
Let us work together to better this world,
my fellow Elders.

113
00:07:29.300 --> 00:07:31.630
Five Elders
St. Figarland Garling
(Godhead of Science & Defense)

114
00:07:37.290 --> 00:07:39.750
St. Saturn, what’s the matter?!

115
00:07:55.220 --> 00:07:56.600
What the hell’s happening?!

116
00:07:56.600 --> 00:07:58.310
Medics! Hurry!

117
00:07:58.310 --> 00:08:01.860
This is terrible! We can’t allow
the world’s highest authority to come to harm!

118
00:08:01.860 --> 00:08:03.360
Sir, have you caught something?

119
00:08:03.360 --> 00:08:05.940
Is there anything we
can do for you, St. Saturn?!

120
00:08:21.130 --> 00:08:24.250
Have I been...?

121
00:08:24.880 --> 00:08:26.380
Great Imu!

122
00:08:26.380 --> 00:08:27.920
I...

123
00:08:27.920 --> 00:08:32.850
Saturn, wherefore hast thou
permitted Joyboy to escape?

124
00:08:32.850 --> 00:08:33.970
mu...

125
00:08:33.970 --> 00:08:35.560
Mercy, please!

126
00:08:36.220 --> 00:08:40.060
I did not know that his powers
were so nebulous!

127
00:08:41.520 --> 00:08:47.440
Great... Imu...

128
00:09:02.540 --> 00:09:04.920
S... St. Saturn?

129
00:09:10.800 --> 00:09:11.470
Bo...

130
00:09:11.880 --> 00:09:12.840
Bones...?

131
00:09:24.860 --> 00:09:27.020
We couldn’t retake the Labophase...

132
00:09:29.030 --> 00:09:32.490
York got in our way! Dammit all!

133
00:09:34.450 --> 00:09:37.490
Our Mental Waves can reach anywhere...

134
00:09:37.490 --> 00:09:39.700
So York still has access here.

135
00:09:39.700 --> 00:09:43.580
Ah getcha, but it’s better than
lettin’ her have da real deal.

136
00:09:43.580 --> 00:09:48.550
Fer now, let’s jus’ watch over dis genius brain of ours
‘til humanity can make proper use of it.

137
00:09:48.550 --> 00:09:52.510
That will take five centuries. Did you make
these island clouds the floating type?

138
00:09:52.510 --> 00:09:56.470
O’ course! Far’s the world’s concerned,
Vegapunk’s dead ‘n gone!

139
00:09:56.470 --> 00:09:58.510
We can go globetrottin’ all we want!

140
00:09:58.510 --> 00:10:02.520
We can’t create inventions because we have
neither the funds nor the materials...

141
00:10:02.980 --> 00:10:05.020
We’ll look to our friends fer dat.

142
00:10:05.480 --> 00:10:06.270
‘Kay, den!

143
00:10:06.250 --> 00:10:08.960
Ta- daah!

144
00:10:08.070 --> 00:10:08.980
Howzat?

145
00:10:10.900 --> 00:10:13.110
You look so ridiculous!

146
00:10:13.110 --> 00:10:15.450
Were you hoping to have
a body type like mine?

147
00:10:15.450 --> 00:10:17.160
Y’all talkin’ outta yer butts!

148
00:10:17.620 --> 00:10:20.370
Toss out York’s body parts!

149
00:10:20.990 --> 00:10:23.120
Good call! Dey’s bad vibes!

150
00:10:25.620 --> 00:10:28.840
Hello? Is this Weatheria?
This is Vegapunk!

151
00:10:28.840 --> 00:10:33.590
What?! What do you want?!
 I thought you were dead!

152
00:10:34.090 --> 00:10:36.970
Oh, I don’t like this!
Hey, what’s gonna happen now?

153
00:10:36.970 --> 00:10:39.600
Are we gonna die?!
I don’t wanna die!

154
00:10:39.580 --> 00:10:44.080
Kama-
bakka
Queen-
dom

155
00:10:39.620 --> 00:10:42.310
I choose life! I’ll swim to live!

156
00:10:43.100 --> 00:10:44.100
So, basically...

157
00:10:44.100 --> 00:10:49.020
a massive war occurred
during the undocumented Void Century,

158
00:10:49.020 --> 00:10:51.730
and the Ancient Weapons
used in that conflict...

159
00:10:51.730 --> 00:10:54.610
caused the world to sink
by 200 meters.

160
00:10:55.070 --> 00:10:59.120
Whoever claims the One Piece and
becomes the King of the Pirates...

161
00:10:59.120 --> 00:11:02.540
will have that power once again!

162
00:11:02.540 --> 00:11:05.000
We can’t just wait for that to happen.

163
00:11:07.040 --> 00:11:09.040
The world sinking into the sea...

164
00:11:09.500 --> 00:11:14.590
The fact that the Celestial Dragons reside
at the world’s highest elevation, the Red Line...

165
00:11:14.590 --> 00:11:16.010
Tequila Wolf.

166
00:11:15.990 --> 00:11:25.960
Tequila Wolf

167
00:11:16.160 --> 00:11:25.960
Vodka Wolf

168
00:11:16.380 --> 00:11:17.470
Vodka Wolf.

169
00:11:17.280 --> 00:11:25.960
Rum Wolf

170
00:11:17.470 --> 00:11:18.510
Rum Wolf.

171
00:11:18.280 --> 00:11:25.960
Bourbon Wolf

172
00:11:18.510 --> 00:11:20.220
Bourbon Wolf.

173
00:11:20.220 --> 00:11:21.640
All of those megastructures

174
00:11:21.640 --> 00:11:25.980
that they’ve had slaves constructing,
going back 700 years!

175
00:11:25.980 --> 00:11:26.980
Yeah...

176
00:11:26.980 --> 00:11:29.690
Yeah, it all starts to make sense.

177
00:11:29.690 --> 00:11:32.070
I was gonna say that!

178
00:11:32.070 --> 00:11:34.150
Oh, I don’t like this!

179
00:11:34.610 --> 00:11:36.150
Vegapunk...

180
00:11:36.150 --> 00:11:39.820
Unfortunately, not all who believed
the words you gave your life to share...

181
00:11:39.820 --> 00:11:43.740
will prepare for
the looming disaster peacefully.

182
00:11:44.830 --> 00:11:47.750
Don’t lose sight of
your target now, Dragon.

183
00:11:47.750 --> 00:11:50.710
This demands a swift resolution.
Otherwise...

184
00:11:51.290 --> 00:11:55.590
people will start fighting
over the safe areas that remain.

185
00:12:00.760 --> 00:12:02.720
She woke up!

186
00:12:02.720 --> 00:12:03.680
Huh...

187
00:12:06.850 --> 00:12:08.020
I...

188
00:12:08.020 --> 00:12:10.350
Whew, what a relief!

189
00:12:10.350 --> 00:12:11.980
You feeling okay, Lilith?

190
00:12:11.980 --> 00:12:13.900
Lilith!

191
00:12:16.780 --> 00:12:17.990
Lilith...

192
00:12:18.860 --> 00:12:22.570
All that said, you’re in a cabin
on the giants’ ship.

193
00:12:22.570 --> 00:12:24.450
Everything’s huge here.

194
00:12:24.450 --> 00:12:25.870
The giants...

195
00:12:26.540 --> 00:12:28.290
Lilith, the thing is...

196
00:12:28.290 --> 00:12:30.000
I hate to say this,

197
00:12:30.000 --> 00:12:34.420
but we failed to get
any other Vegapunks out besides you.

198
00:12:35.090 --> 00:12:36.300
I’m so sorry.

199
00:12:38.300 --> 00:12:42.220
Atlas was the one who knocked you out,
but I think she did it in order to...

200
00:12:42.220 --> 00:12:45.600
It’s fine. I know.
I’ve just been informed of everything.

201
00:12:45.600 --> 00:12:48.310
“Just been informed”? By who?

202
00:12:52.190 --> 00:12:55.320
Just give me a minute to cry.

203
00:13:00.950 --> 00:13:04.450
What about you is evil, exactly?

204
00:13:05.410 --> 00:13:06.330
I’m hungry!

205
00:13:06.330 --> 00:13:07.620
You recover quick!

206
00:13:07.620 --> 00:13:12.580
Well, then... If you’re hungry,
the giants set out fruit for us on the table.

207
00:13:13.000 --> 00:13:16.420
Come over once you’ve calmed down.
I’ll wait for you there.

208
00:13:17.250 --> 00:13:18.210
Now...

209
00:13:18.210 --> 00:13:21.470
why am I getting so hungry?

210
00:13:21.470 --> 00:13:21.930
Oh!

211
00:13:21.930 --> 00:13:24.590
Must be because my brain’s
no longer linked with York’s.

212
00:13:25.390 --> 00:13:28.640
Good to see you, Lilith!
I see you’ve come to!

213
00:13:29.020 --> 00:13:30.810
Is the grub up there?

214
00:13:30.810 --> 00:13:31.600
“Grub”?

215
00:13:31.600 --> 00:13:33.310
Oh, you mean food.

216
00:13:33.310 --> 00:13:35.790
It’s rather depressing up there...

217
00:13:34.420 --> 00:13:36.630
Sulk

218
00:13:35.810 --> 00:13:37.400
Oh? Why’s that?

219
00:13:37.400 --> 00:13:40.610
Damm ih! Ah promished ‘im...

220
00:13:40.610 --> 00:13:42.280
Are you okay?

221
00:13:45.320 --> 00:13:48.030
Oh, Lilith... Luffy’s really
down about it, too.

222
00:13:48.030 --> 00:13:50.540
He’s so depressed,
he’s losing his appetite...

223
00:13:50.540 --> 00:13:54.710
I promised Apple Gramps
I’d help ‘im escape...

224
00:13:54.710 --> 00:13:56.500
Gramps...!

225
00:13:56.500 --> 00:13:59.000
He’s only eaten
five bunches of grapes...

226
00:13:59.000 --> 00:14:00.090
He’s had plenty!

227
00:14:01.130 --> 00:14:04.430
I see... That’s why you’re depressed.

228
00:14:04.430 --> 00:14:06.430
But don’t be!

229
00:14:06.430 --> 00:14:08.390
I’ve just been informed...

230
00:14:08.850 --> 00:14:10.810
“Just”?

231
00:14:10.810 --> 00:14:13.770
You keep telling us you’ve “been informed”.
What do you mean by that?

232
00:14:13.770 --> 00:14:17.940
The reason I cried earlier is because
I’m saddened by everyone’s deaths.

233
00:14:17.940 --> 00:14:21.440
But that’s only according to
your definition of death.

234
00:14:22.110 --> 00:14:24.400
The truth is, simply put...

235
00:14:25.610 --> 00:14:27.370
They’re all alive!

236
00:14:31.330 --> 00:14:36.080
WHAAAA?!

237
00:14:36.580 --> 00:14:39.040
But to you, they’re dead!

238
00:14:39.920 --> 00:14:41.000
Nope, don’t get it!

239
00:14:41.000 --> 00:14:42.260
You mean they’re ghosts?

240
00:14:42.260 --> 00:14:43.210
Horrifying!

241
00:14:43.210 --> 00:14:44.510
Rich, comin’ from you!

242
00:14:44.970 --> 00:14:47.090
What I’m trying to say...

243
00:14:47.090 --> 00:14:50.560
is that you guys kept your word!

244
00:14:51.680 --> 00:14:52.520
So...

245
00:14:53.480 --> 00:14:55.310
don’t be so down, Luffy!

246
00:14:56.810 --> 00:14:58.610
I don’t really get it, but...

247
00:14:59.150 --> 00:15:01.690
you mean Apple Gramps is still there?

248
00:15:02.110 --> 00:15:04.030
Yup, sure is!

249
00:15:05.900 --> 00:15:09.160
Quit asking what’s real and what’s not!

250
00:15:09.160 --> 00:15:11.330
You decide for yourself!

251
00:15:11.330 --> 00:15:15.460
If you ask me, that concept
is just a relic of the past!

252
00:15:20.130 --> 00:15:24.130
